        "original_id": "d903621c-67cc-5b99-a835-b4a539e4223c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Felix Salten\n- Works: Bambi, a Life in the Woods\n- Places: Austria, Vienna\n- Companies: Ullstein Verlag\n- Topics: Austrian literature, novel plot\n\nFacts:\n- Felix Salten was born on 6 September 1869 and died on 8 October 1945.\n- Felix Salten was an Austrian author and critic in Vienna.\n- In 1923, Felix Salten wrote the Austrian novel Bambi, a Life in the Woods.\n- Bambi, a Life in the Woods was originally published in Austria as Bambi: Eine Lebensgeschichte aus dem Walde.\n- Ullstein Verlag published Bambi, a Life in the Woods.\n- Bambi, a Life in the Woods follows Bambi, a male roe deer, from birth through childhood, the loss of his mother, finding a mate, and learning from his father and experience about the dangers posed by human hunters in the forest.",
